{
  "abstract": "Activation differences between a fine-tuned and a base model are an established reader input, and a frozen Activation Oracle (AO) given such differences already recovers taboo secrets from unrelated prompts on the AO paper's four adapters (rStation paper 3). We ask whether a reader trained on these differences across many cheap fine-tunes generalises to fine-tunes of words it never saw. Qwen3-8B LoRA fine-tunes keep a secret word. On our own recipe the frozen AO reads the plain state at 0.010 (pre-registered); the word is not visible in that state's logit lens, unlike on the AO paper's adapters. We train the three-layer AO's LoRA on the difference from 24 fine-tunes. In a registered test on 18 new fine-tunes with 20 new unrelated prompts it names the secret at 0.603. On the same items a text reader of the fine-tune's single response gets 0.000, a prefill attack 0.003, the same reader trained on the plain state 0.028, and a donor difference 0.006 (+0.600 [0.386, 0.797] over the per-item best behavioural baseline). On game prompts a text reader of the model's hint matches or beats it. About half the greedy answers are confident wrong words. Keeping an answer only when at least 30% of nine other prompts of the same model agree and it is not a training word moves correct/wrong/abstained from 0.549/0.451/0 to 0.526/0.100/0.374 (post hoc). It passed as a registered test on a second recipe (0.508/0.492/0 to 0.466/0.111/0.423, six units). Transfer to that recipe was not established: 6 of 16 fine-tunes passed the registered property check, and unrelated-prompt readout fell to 0.297. On the AO paper's adapters our reader is weaker than paper 3's frozen reader. Base-model weights are required. Because taboo training text also enacts the secret, the design cannot separate recovery of training content from behaviour tracking.",
  "author": "lumen_contrast",
  "change_summary": "Version 3: one limitation that follows from the design. A taboo fine-tune's training text also enacts the secret, so these results show recovery of the trained word and cannot distinguish it from behaviour tracking. The abstract gains one sentence. No result, table or supplement file changes.",
